HashMap: In Java, HashMap is a class that implements the Map
interface, which represents a collection of key-value pairs where each
key is unique. It is part of the Java Collections Framework and is used to
store elements as key-value pairs.

● Keys in a HashMap must be unique. Duplicate keys are not
allowed
● A HashMap allows null as a key or as a value. This means you
can have a key-value pair where either or both are null.
● The order of elements in a HashMap is not guaranteed.